apklayer patch: ShadowView.performHapticFeedback(int) runs View's own code (ViewRootImpl, then the vibrator_manager's haptic feedback in HubVibrator)
instead of only recording the constant and answering true: an app's View.performHapticFeedback reaches the vibrator HAL as on Android.
Against external/robolectric 87aa52b08 (REVISION). Applied by runtime/meson.build onto the staged
upstream sources (<native>/aosp/robolectric-src); the result is compiled into native-runtime.jar ahead of Robolectric_all.jar.
---
--- a/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowView.java
+++ b/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowView.java
@@ -891,6 +891,9 @@
     void setOnTouchListener(View.OnTouchListener onTouchListener);
 
     @Direct
+    boolean performHapticFeedback(int hapticFeedbackType);  // apklayer patch
+
+    @Direct
     boolean post(Runnable action);
 
     @Direct
@@ -971,7 +974,7 @@
   @Implementation
   protected boolean performHapticFeedback(int hapticFeedbackType) {
     hapticFeedbackPerformed = hapticFeedbackType;
-    return true;
+    return reflector(ViewReflector.class, realView).performHapticFeedback(hapticFeedbackType);  // apklayer patch: the real view's, to the vibrator
   }
 
   @Implementation
